[17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186431011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating an Eigenvector Corresponding to a Given Eigenvalue" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186128939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "4def2d61-0093-53cf-bcbb-1d2c3e6e1738" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186381111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186392038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Eigenvectors of a 3x3 Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186128940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "8e732a2b-a6a1-5e0f-b43e-a9fbc02cfc74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129325 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186129963 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129325 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186129964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129325 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186129965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129325 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186129966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129325 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129325 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129325 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating the Eigenvectors of a 3x3 Matrix With Distinct Eigenvalues" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129325 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186129963 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129325 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129325 #edb/ref 1050 1020.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129325 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "0e238e7b-3085-5b87-b3c4-0f5c35258e51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129963 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129963 #edb/ref 1061 20099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129963 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "875dc5aa-e4f4-50f8-a30e-d5ed46d77e32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129963 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129964 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129964 #edb/ref 1061 20100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129964 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "59537f37-7060-5544-9b4a-84501e450c50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129964 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129965 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129965 #edb/ref 1061 20101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129965 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8a926ac2-afd2-5b57-8911-c3b8dac86d39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129965 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129966 #edb/ref 1061 20102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129966 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5d1fcdf4-d676-5ff5-bf31-d7e371f43f08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129966 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130084 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130084 #edb/ref 1061 27265 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130084 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3314b023-f15c-5f8b-a4e4-aeea702377a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130084 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130347 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the following $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n![](images/4f/4fd591d8028847aa7e1d11e840acdb192703d152f9c397e40fec98fd1e281c41.svg)\n\nIf we are told that one of the eigenvalues of this matrix is $\\lambda = 3,$ how do we calculate the corresponding eigenvector?\n\nTo compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation\n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =3.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find the eigenvectors, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this reduced matrix, there are two pivot columns (the $2$nd and $3$rd). Thus, $x_1$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we have $x_3 = 0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain $x_2 = 0.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n![](images/70/705dd92c7330897f35671b66866791160b9d7f65e3280d5ccb9d992405c08942.svg)\n\nSetting $x_1=1,$ we get the following eigenvector:\n\n![](images/2a/2a5dd6c35fb81134f13e765e0a02be4ea2feedfd878a1923491813492739ef00.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186130347 #edb/ref 1065 3566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130347 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b1a9d148-15f7-5878-8f36-f19ee99c49d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130347 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130403 #edb/ref 1064 "Note the following important theorem.\n\n*The set of eigenvectors $\\{ \\mathbf{v}_1,\\mathbf{v}_2, \\ldots, \\mathbf{v}_k \\}$ of a matrix $A,$ where each vector $\\mathbf v_i$ corresponds to a different eigenvalue, is linearly independent.*\n\n**Watch out!** Eigenvectors that correspond to the *same* eigenvalue *can* be (and very often *will* be) linearly dependent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130403 #edb/ref 1065 4432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130403 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c0f0f6d3-c9e1-52a6-bf51-244bb7751a9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130403 #edb/ref 1067 "Eigenvectors That Correspond to Different Eigenvalues" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163546 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186163547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163546 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186163548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163546 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186163549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163546 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186163550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163546 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186163551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163546 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163546 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163546 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186163550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163546 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5b75e96e-6286-569e-8a97-9f97357e7c1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] 